    "lawCode": "Add §9-a, Vol Ffs Ben L; add §9-a, Vol Amb Wkr Ben L",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer Firefighters' Benefit Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1318\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the volunteer firefighters' benefit law and the volun-\nteer ambulance workers' benefit law, in relation to updating benefits\nand modernizing coverage for services provided in the line of duty\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation updates and modernizes certain provisions of law relat-\ning to the volunteer fire service. The purpose of the legislation is to\nmore accurately reflect current emergency response practices and to\nbring the state of the law for volunteers into greater parity with other\nsegments of the response community.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the volunteer firefighters' benefit law (VFBL) to\nprovide a weekly benefit of $650 for volunteers that sustain total\npermanent disability or partial permanent disability while in the line\nof duty.\n\nSection 2 amends the volunteer ambulance workers' benefit law (VAWBL) to\nprovide a weekly benefit of $650 for volunteers that sustain total\npermanent disability or partial permanent disability while in the line\nof duty.\n\nSection 3 establishes effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLike any other industry, the volunteer fire service has evolved over\ntime. Years of experience and technological advancements have changed\nthe ways volunteer emergency response is provided and, as a result, a\nnew set of preferred or best practices has developed. This legislation\nis designed to modernize the law to better reflect current practices and\nto update the law to bring the volunteer fire service into greater pari-\nty with other segments of the workforce.\n\nDespite years of experience and technological advancements, injuries are\nstill a part of the volunteer fire service. Sometimes the injuries are\nsevere - causing temporary or total permanent disabilities. The weekly\nbenefit under VFBL and VAWBL for such injuries has not been updated in\nover ten years. It is time to update these benefits.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S4631A/A5895,\n2017-2018: S3904A/A.6367-A,\n2015-2016: S2719A/A.1627,\n2013-2014: S3589B/A485-B,\n2011-2012: S5624B/A.8563-B\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nNone to the State. This bill may affect premiums of local districts that\npurchase policies in accordance with the VFBL or the VAWBL.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
